{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And now.</b> Since You have agreed that I myself shall be the angel." "<b>Make known to me, I pray, Your ways.</b> Make known to me Your two wondrous ways. The first: how by Your knowledge alone You bestow existence upon existents, as explained in the Guide. The second: how through Your knowledge, which never errs regarding future things, the nature of possibility and free choice nevertheless remains in them." "<b>That I may know You.</b> For truly through knowledge of the actions there will be some knowledge of the form from which those actions are derived." "<b>That I may find favor in Your eyes.</b> For through this I shall find favor and good intellect in the eyes of Elohim, as it says: כִּי אִם בְּזֹאת יִתְהַלֵּל הַמִּתְהַלֵּל, הַשְׂכֵּל וְיָדֹעַ אוֹתִי כִּי בְאֵלֶּה חָפַצְתִּי (Jeremiah 9:23)." "<b>And see that this nation is Your people.</b> For Your name is known among them and not among the nations, as it says: נוֹדַע בִּיהוּדָה אֱלֹהִים וגו׳ (Psalms 76:2). If so, it is not fitting that You withhold from me what I have asked on account of their sin — as they said, of blessed memory (Sukkah 45a), that thirty of them are worthy that the Shekhinah should rest upon them as upon Moses our teacher, except that the generation is not worthy of it."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:58.275601061Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}